# Global Definition of Done (applies to ALL sprints)

A sprint is only complete when:

## Code Quality
- Feature implementation is complete and works end-to-end
- Code follows service-layer architecture (no business logic in UI)
- TypeScript types are defined for new domain objects
- No direct fetch calls exist in React components (services must be used)

## Testing
- Unit tests added or updated where applicable
- API or integration tests added for backend changes
- E2E tests added for critical user flows (if applicable)
- Tests pass in CI (or locally if CI not yet enabled)

## Documentation
- Relevant documentation updated (see `.cursor/rules/30-documentation.mdc` mapping rules)
- README updated if user-facing behavior changed
- Roadmap updated to reflect sprint progress (`docs/roadmap/AI-INVESTOR-ROADMAP.md`)
- Sprint progress tracker updated (`docs/quality/SPRINT-X-CLOSEOUT.md`)
- ADR created for any architectural decision

## Verification
- Behavior changes verified against the running application (see `CLAUDE.md` and `.cursor/rules/ironbee-devtools-use.mdc`)
- Docs-only or design-doc work does not satisfy code epic completion without implementation + tests

## Engineering Discipline
- No duplicate logic introduced
- No unnecessary dependencies added
- Clear separation between UI, service, provider, and data layers
- Meaningful commit messages are used

## AI Usage Integrity
- Any AI-generated code has been reviewed and validated
- AI-generated logic is refactored if necessary for clarity or correctness

